# Which second languages a skill description must carry triggers in.
#
# One entry per line. Commas also separate entries; `|` inside one entry accepts
# any of its labels, so `한국어|Korean` passes for a description that marks its
# Korean triggers in either script. Blank lines and `#` comments are ignored.
#
# This is a property of THIS deployment, not of the harness: a contributor
# writing a skill for a Japanese team should not need a Korean marker to pass
# CI. Change this file, not scripts/verify-frontmatter.sh.
#
# It is a file rather than a Makefile variable because Windows `make.exe`
# re-encodes recipe text through the ANSI codepage on its way into the child
# environment, which turned `한국어` into mojibake and failed five skills that
# plainly carry the marker. A file is read straight as UTF-8 by the one program
# that needs it, so nothing re-encodes it.
한국어|Korean
